}]},{"verse_key":"11:10","surah":11,"ayah":10,"ar_uthmani":"وَلَئِنْ أَذَقْنَـٰهُ نَعْمَآءَ بَعْدَ ضَرَّآءَ مَسَّتْهُ لَيَقُولَنَّ ذَهَبَ ٱلسَّيِّـَٔاتُ عَنِّىٓ ۚ إِنَّهُۥ لَفَرِحٌ فَخُورٌ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"And if We let him taste mercy after some harm has touched him, he is sure to say, ‘Misfortune has gone away from me.’ He becomes exultant and boastful.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"وَلَئِنْ","en_gloss":"But if","transliteration":"wala-in","verse_key":"11:10"},{"pos":2,"ar":"أَذَقْنَـٰهُ","en_gloss":"We give him a taste","transliteration":"adhaqnāhu","verse_key":"11:10"},{"pos":3,"ar":"نَعْمَآءَ","en_gloss":"(of) favor","transliteration":"naʿmāa","verse_key":"11:10"},{"pos":4,"ar":"بَعْدَ","en_gloss":"after","transliteration":"baʿda","verse_key":"11:10"},{"pos":5,"ar":"ضَرَّآءَ","en_gloss":"hardship","transliteration":"ḍarrāa","verse_key":"11:10"},{"pos":6,"ar":"مَسَّتْهُ","en_gloss":"(has) touched him","transliteration":"massathu","verse_key":"11:10"},{"pos":7,"ar":"لَيَقُولَنَّ","en_gloss":"surely, he will say","transliteration":"layaqūlanna","verse_key":"11:10"},{"pos":8,"ar":"ذَهَبَ","en_gloss":"Have gone","transliteration":"dhahaba","verse_key":"11:10"},{"pos":9,"ar":"ٱلسَّيِّـَٔاتُ","en_gloss":"the evils","transliteration":"l-sayiātu","verse_key":"11:10"},{"pos":10,"ar":"عَنِّىٓ ۚ","en_gloss":"from me","transliteration":"ʿannī","verse_key":"11:10"},{"pos":11,"ar":"إِنَّهُۥ","en_gloss":"Indeed, he","transliteration":"innahu","verse_key":"11:10"},{"pos":12,"ar":"لَفَرِحٌۭ","en_gloss":"(is) exultant","transliteration":"lafariḥun","verse_key":"11:10"},{"pos":13,"ar":"فَخُورٌ","en_gloss":"(and) boastful","transliteration":"fakhūrun","verse_key":"11:10"},{"pos":14,"ar":"١٠","en_gloss":"(10)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"11:10"}]},{"verse_key":"11:11","surah":11,"ayah":11,"ar_uthmani":"إِلَّا ٱلَّذِينَ صَبَرُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّـٰلِحَـٰتِ أُو۟لَـٰٓئِكَ لَهُم مَّغْفِرَةٌ وَأَجْرٌ كَبِيرٌ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"Not so those who are steadfast and do good deeds: they will have forgiveness and a great reward.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"إِلَّا","en_gloss":"Except","transliteration":"illā","verse_key":"11:11"},{"pos":2,"ar":"ٱلَّذِينَ","en_gloss":"those who","transliteration":"alladhīna","verse_key":"11:11"},{"pos":3,"ar":"صَبَرُوا۟","en_gloss":"(are) patient","transliteration":"ṣabarū","verse_key":"11:11"},{"pos":4,"ar":"وَعَمِلُوا۟","en_gloss":"and do","transliteration":"waʿamilū","verse_key":"11:11"},{"pos":5,"ar":"ٱلصَّـٰلِحَـٰتِ","en_gloss":"the good deeds","transliteration":"l-ṣāliḥāti","verse_key":"11:11"},{"pos":6,"ar":"أُو۟لَـٰٓئِكَ","en_gloss":"those","transliteration":"ulāika","verse_key":"11:11"},{"pos":7,"ar":"لَهُم","en_gloss":"for them","transliteration":"lahum","verse_key":"11:11"},{"pos":8,"ar":"مَّغْفِرَةٌۭ","en_gloss":"(will be) forgiveness","transliteration":"maghfiratun","verse_key":"11:11"},{"pos":9,"ar":"وَأَجْرٌۭ","en_gloss":"and a reward","transliteration":"wa-ajrun","verse_key":"11:11"},{"pos":10,"ar":"كَبِيرٌۭ","en_gloss":"great","transliteration":"kabīrun","verse_key":"11:11"},{"pos":11,"ar":"١١","en_gloss":"(11)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"11:11"}]},{"verse_key":"11:12","surah":11,"ayah":12,"ar_uthmani":"فَلَعَلَّكَ تَارِكٌۢ بَعْضَ مَا يُوحَىٰٓ إِلَيْكَ وَضَآئِقٌۢ بِهِۦ صَدْرُكَ أَن يَقُولُوا۟ لَوْلَآ أُنزِلَ عَلَيْهِ كَنزٌ أَوْ جَآءَ مَعَهُۥ مَلَكٌ ۚ إِنَّمَآ أَنتَ نَذِيرٌ ۚ وَٱللَّهُ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ وَكِيلٌ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"So [Prophet] are you going to abandon some part of what is revealed to you, and let your heart be oppressed by it, because they say, ‘Why is no treasure sent down to him? Why has no angel come with him?’? You are only there to warn; it is God who is in charge of everything.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"فَلَعَلَّكَ","en_gloss":"Then possibly you","transliteration":"falaʿallaka","verse_key":"11:12"},{"pos":2,"ar":"تَارِكٌۢ","en_gloss":"(may) give up","transliteration":"tārikun","verse_key":"11:12"},{"pos":3,"ar":"بَعْضَ","en_gloss":"a par